---
import Layout from "@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import ContentGuide from "@/components/Item/ContentGuide.astro";
const content = {
  eyebrow: "Architecture",
  title: "One computer. A clear boundary.",
  intro:
    "The app runs where the sources live. Local processes and Docker containers work together within one installation.",
  sections: [
    {
      id: "single-machine",
      title: "Your local application",
      paragraphs: [
        "The browser UI and Hono API run together on localhost:5173. A local SQLite database holds the index, settings, history, and evidence records. The default Docker volume retains this data across container restarts.",
        "Docker publishes only to loopback. Native development and production bind to loopback. The API rejects remote hostnames and foreign browser origins before executing requests. This is a personal application with no multi-user authentication.",
      ],
    },
    {
      id: "sources",
      title: "Explicit filesystem access",
      paragraphs: [
        "Selected source folders are mounted read-only into the container. You then register their container paths in Knowledge resources. Indexing copies extracted text into the local SQLite index; original files are not uploaded to the product web host.",
        "Browser profiles follow the same explicit grant. The UI lets you choose which discovered profiles to import. Native installations can discover accessible profiles on the same machine.",
      ],
    },
    {
      id: "compute",
      title: "Your choice of AI endpoint",
      paragraphs: [
        "The index stays on this computer. AI connects through an independently selected profile: a local Lemonade, LM Studio, Ollama, or llama.cpp runtime, a private gateway such as Blade, or another compatible HTTP(S) endpoint.",
        "The selected endpoint and whether it is local or remote are visible in the app. Selecting remote AI sends prompts, conversation context, and retrieved excerpts to it. KeepIndex never automatically switches between local and remote connections.",
      ],
      link: {
        href: "/inference",
        label: "Connect local AI",
      },
    },
    {
      id: "internet",
      title: "The web is still the web",
      paragraphs: [
        "SearXNG runs in a container on the same computer. When you include web results, it sends search terms to public engines, and KeepIndex can fetch source pages. Those destinations receive normal network requests.",
        "Choose Files, Vaults, Docs, or History to retrieve that local source category without web discovery. All and Web explicitly include public engines.",
      ],
    },
    {
      id: "devices",
      title: "What happens on another device",
      paragraphs: [
        "Opening keepindex.ing on a phone shows this product site. It does not pair with your laptop or expose its files. Another computer can run its own independent KeepIndex installation.",
        "Federation, remote viewing, source agents, and network-wide discovery are deferred. An OS-mounted network share can look like a normal folder, but indexing it would copy extracted content to the indexing computer; it is not source-resident federation.",
      ],
    },
    {
      id: "hosting",
      title: "Product hosting is separate",
      paragraphs: [
        "The product website is a static build on a separate web host. It holds public website assets only.",
        "Your personal installation runs on your computer. Visiting the product website does not expose it or connect it to the web host.",
      ],
    },
  ],
};
---

<Layout title={content.title} description={content.intro}
  ><ContentGuide {...content} /></Layout
>
